 "notes": "Please check:\n1. Maidens (most important; 173+ observations): 'South Maidens' headings run 1882-1887, but before 1887 the station lists print only 'Maidens', and stations.json files that under maidens-north. maidens-south is seen only in 1887. I gave all 'South Maidens' items maidens-south, so the 1882-86 'Maidens' list entry probably belongs to maidens-south (or a combined id). Check before the year-consistency test flags these.\n2. Unresolved, ids left empty: n=69 'Arklow West Light-ship' (1884; North or South?) and n=1057 'Rowe' (1886).\n3. Speculative OCR readings: n=922 'Niiyband' as Kish Bank; n=983 'Pasta!' as Fastnet; n=1116 'No he' as North.\n4. Eagle Island tower letters: I read H, K, L and '#' as a garbled E, because E garbles in this OCR (Hagle, Kagle, Lagle) while W survives. Read this way: n=332, 333, 334 (letter lost), 338 ('S.' in 1885), 522, 655. Bare island names (n=331, 339, 1379) and bare 'Slyne Head' 1886 (n=1115) are given both stations. Narrow them if the page shows which tower.\n5. n=70 bare 'Arran Island' 1886: assigned to North (eeragh) because the other 1886 Arran headings are North.\n6. n=845 'Mew Island' 1882-83: before the 1884 move the Copeland light was not on Mew Island. I resolved it to copeland, but strictly it is a nearby place.\n7. Nearby places, probably remarks inside a station's report: n=182 Bull Rock and n=268 Cow Rock (likely Dursey Island), n=1503 the Saltees (likely Coningbeg L.V.), n=265 Corclough Lake (identified as Corclogh, Erris, Co. Mayo — uncertain).\n8. n=1198 St John Point: assumed Co. Down; St John's Point in Co. Donegal is also possible.\n9. Also: stations.json has inisheer printing 'Straw Island, S.,' and eeragh printing 'Arran Island, Is.'. These look like list OCR errors; worth confirming they are not separate stations.",
